    {
      "id": "allergic_to",
      "target": "Soy alérgico ___.",
      "pronunciation_easy": "soy ah-LEHR-hee-koh",
      "qa": "Back-translation: \"I am allergic to ___.\" Masculine speaker (file convention); a woman says \"Soy alérgica a ___\" (ah-LEHR-hee-kah). a + el contracts to al (al gluten, al maní), so the article goes with the word, not the frame. Safety item: please verify. Word notes: peanuts = \"maní\" (most of Latin America), \"cacahuate\" (Mexico), \"cacahuete\" (Spain). Nuts = \"frutos secos\" (tree nuts generally); \"nueces\" strictly means walnuts but is used loosely in Mexico. Back-translations of examples: \"I am allergic to the nuts / the peanut / the gluten / the shellfish / the milk / the eggs\" (Spanish uses the article here). Dairy = \"los lácteos\". [Fixed 2026-10-14 per ChatGPT review.]"
    },
    {
      "id": "vegetarian",
